# Team PA within Fund Formation and Sponsor Solutions

Apply for role



### We are recruiting a Team PA to join our Fund Formation & Sponsor Solutions group.

## About Macfarlanes

Macfarlanes is a pre-eminent law firm that serves a global client base in private capital, private wealth, M&A and disputes. Personal connection, an entrepreneurial spirit and a commitment to excellence are at the heart of our firm. These values drive our ability to deliver exceptional outcomes for our clients.

We are big enough to undertake the most complex and demanding mandates yet small enough to know each other well and to be agile, adapting to the needs of our clients. We seek to strengthen the firm by recruiting talented people from all backgrounds who want to build long-lasting and impactful careers with us. Our culture is challenging and supportive, creating an environment where individuals can thrive.

## What this means for you

Joining Macfarlanes means being part of a collaborative, approachable team who want you to succeed. You’ll be encouraged to get involved and be recognised for your contribution.

We take your development seriously. Our learning and development programmes are second to none and are designed to help you strengthen your skills.

Above all, you’ll be part of a firm where we all work together as part of a cohesive and supportive team, value your efforts and help you to thrive.

## The team

Our Fund Formation & Sponsor Solutions group consists of eight Partners, two Senior Counsel, 20 Associates, five Trainee Solicitors, one Senior Advisor, 15 Paralegals and one Senior Knowledge Lawyer. The practice is supported by a team of PAs which consists of one Senior Team PA, one Team PA and two Junior Team PAs.

## The role

The Team PA is an integral part of the practice. They need to be adaptable, dynamic, and confident in their ability to support change, influence and build relationships.

The Team PA will provide an efficient, client focused, professional legal support service to the partners and fee earners within the practice:

Key duties will include:

* provide a high level of tailored support to partners and fee earners and act as the first point of contact;
* adding value by taking a proactive approach to tasks and anticipating potential problems before they arise;
* act as a role model to junior members of the team by sharing knowledge and demonstrating best practice;
* proactively managing a varied workload, with the ability to prioritise and manage partner/fee earner expectations in relation to deadlines and status of tasks;
* working from the team hub;
* complex diary and inbox management for partners, and where necessary send holding responses and proactively resolve potential clashes when scheduling meetings;
* organising internal and external meetings, effectively ensuring rooms and conference facilities are booked, liaising with attendees and ensuring that any required catering and technical equipment is in place, preparation of agendas and collating meetings papers in a timely manner;
* build an understanding of the fee earners work pressures and assist them to meet client demands and develop a knowledge of key clients;
* arranging complex travel bookings, including producing itineraries, obtaining visas, flights, taxis, accommodation and rental cars etc;
* understanding and leading the end-to-end billing process including generating accurate billing reports, draft bills, disbursements, amending narratives and raising credit notes in a timely manner;
* proactively assist the partners/fee-earners with the collections process including drafting and sending emails to clients for outstanding invoices;
* managing accounts payable (invoices), expenses and disbursements;
* understanding the client matter opening process and using our file management system to run conflict searches, open matters, liaising with the risk team on client due diligence requirements, ensuring all relevant documents are filed electronically, file closure and archiving;
* assisting on ad-hoc projects as and when required, for example managing bundles, organising and assisting with client functions, seminars etc;
* managing group and fee earner contacts and BD activities to ensure they are up to date through our CRM InterAction;
* utilising document production and ensuring that all typing, document formatting and redaction work is sent with clear instructions and deadlines; and
* proactively build relationships across the firm and assist across practice groups when required.

Please note that the job description is not exhaustive and may vary in line with changes in the team’s objectives and firm’s policy. This could include providing support to other practice areas during busy periods.

During the first six months of employment, you may be required to attend the office four days per week to support onboarding, training and collaboration. Your line manager may adjust this requirement based on your progress and business needs.

## The candidate

Broadly, we want to recruit an individual that fulfils the following criteria:

**Qualifications, experience and technical skills**

* ideally four years’ experience working as a PA in a law firm or professional services firm;
* secretarial qualifications desirable e.g. RSA, Cilex, legal secretarial diploma or equivalent;
* knowledge of Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel and PowerPoint;
* accurate typing, spelling, grammar and proof-reading skills; and
* strong level of numeracy.

**Personal attributes**

* excellent communication skills and good people skills;
* must be a team player, whilst also being keen to take responsibility for their own duties;
* excellent organisational and administrative skills with the ability to prioritise tasks to meet deadlines;
* adaptable and flexible in an ever-evolving role;
* self-motivated and proactive, able to act on their own initiative and problem solve;
* client-orientated approach, both internally and externally;
* proven ability to work under pressure and meet deadlines whilst maintaining an excellent attention to detail; and
* a professional and presentable manner.

## Application screening

Any offer of employment with us is subject to our pre-employment checks which are conducted by a third-party screening provider. These checks will be initiated with your consent, and your CV will be sent to the provider by us. The screening will include but is not limited to your employment references, professional and academic qualifications including grades and any criminal records. Your offer will be subject to the successful completion of these checks.

## Our commitment to inclusion

Inclusion is one of our key priorities and it is a goal we are actively working towards. We believe that an inclusive, forward-thinking culture is intrinsically important and enables us to provide innovative solutions to our clients.

We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, bringing different perspectives and experiences, making Macfarlanes an exciting and stimulating place to work. We seek to recruit the best candidates, regardless of age, gender, race, ethnicity, social or economic background, religion, disability, sexual orientation or any other characteristic.

As part of this commitment, we will ask you certain diversity data questions. We would really appreciate you and/or your recruiter completing these questions when submitting an application to Macfarlanes as this data enables us to measure our progress and identify any actions needed to continue to support an inclusive culture. This data is anonymised to maintain the privacy of applicants. If you have any questions relating to how this data is used, please contact a member of the recruitment team.

Should you require any adjustments during the application and/or interview process, please do not hesitate to inform your recruiter or a member of the recruitment team. Please note, the job description is available in other accessible formats (for example, large print).

We are a Disability Confident Employer and will offer an interview to disabled applicants who best meet the essential criteria for the role. If you would like to apply through the Disability Confident Interview Scheme, please email the recruitment team at recruitment@macfarlanes.com.

# Materials Engineer, Optical Substrate

Abingdon

Full time

Posted 0 days ago

R0046933

Apply Now

Snap Inc is a technology company. We believe the camera presents the greatest opportunity to improve the way people live and communicate. Snap contributes to human progress by empowering people to express themselves, live in the moment, learn about the world, and have fun together.



The Company operates Snapchat, a visual messaging app that enhances your relationships with friends, family, and the world, and Specs Inc., a wholly-owned subsidiary dedicated to making computing more human, in addition to Bitmoji, Saturn, and other digital services.



Specs Inc. is a wholly-owned subsidiary of Snap Inc. dedicated to making computing more human. The company develops Specs, advanced eyewear that seamlessly integrates digital experiences into the physical world.



Specs feature see-through lenses that place digital objects directly into three-dimensional space, powered by Snap OS, a proprietary, context-aware operating system designed for natural interaction with your hands and voice.



Specs Inc. also provides Lens Studio, a full suite of advanced developer tools that powers immersive augmented reality experiences across Specs, Snapchat, and other services.



We are looking for a Nanophotonics Engineer to develop, qualify, and scale optical materials, waveguide processes, and measurement methodologies for next-generation augmented reality devices.



This role combines materials qualification with optical simulation, hands-on fabrication, metrology, mechanical and reliability testing, and technical engagement with suppliers. You will work across the complete development lifecycle: defining requirements, planning experiments, fabricating and measuring samples, benchmarking results against simulations, identifying root causes, and translating findings into robust product and manufacturing decisions.



**What you’ll do:**

* Lead or support material and substrate qualification across polymers, glass, lithium niobate, silicon carbide, and other advanced optical materials;
* Define sample requirements, test plans, acceptance criteria, and data packages for internal and external technical initiatives;
* Perform and interpret optical measurements, including transmission, reflectance, refractive index, absorption, haze, scattering, efficiency, uniformity, luminance, MTF, and FOV;
* Establish measurement methods and evaluate metrology capability for surface roughness, flatness, scattering, visual inspection, and wafer-level optical characterization;
* Plan and execute experiments comparing optical simulations with measured performance, identifying discrepancies and closing the loop through design or process revisions;
* Develop and refine fabrication processes, including wafer cleaning, nanoimprinting, thin-film coating, laser cutting, blackening, and waveguide stacking;
* Develop reliability and mechanical test strategies covering flexural strength, impact and drop resistance, thermal exposure, UV weathering, humidity, dynamic fatigue, adhesion, and geometric stability;
* Translate optical and process requirements into supplier-ready drawings, wafer layouts, mask data, cutting instructions, and technical specifications;
* Collaborate directly with material, coating, wafer, and equipment suppliers to qualify capabilities, review technical data, manage samples, and resolve process challenges;
* Coordinate cross-functional builds and trials alongside materials, process, design, manufacturing, reliability, and optical-test engineering teams;
* Analyze experimental data, maintain rigorous technical documentation, and communicate key insights and recommendations to stakeholders and leadership.



**Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities**

* Strong core fundamentals in optics, nanophotonics, mechanics, waveguide physics, or optical materials;
* Proven track record of designing and executing experiments in R&D or manufacturing environments;
* Ability to correlate optical performance with material properties, process parameters, structural geometry, and measurement uncertainty;
* Exceptional data analysis and problem-solving skills, with a proven capability to isolate design, process, material, and metrology variables;
* Practical expertise in optical measurement systems and experimental calibration techniques;
* Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with internal stakeholders and external partners;
* High attention to detail in sample handling, process control, data traceability, and technical documentation.



**Minimum Qualifications**

* PhD in Physics, Photonics, Optical Engineering, Materials Science, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or a related technical discipline, or 7+ years of relevant industry experience;
* Hands-on experience with optical experimentation, materials characterization, photonic device development, or a related laboratory discipline;
* Experience analyzing complex experimental data and delivering technical recommendations;
* Ability to create structured test plans, document procedures, and maintain traceable experimental records;
* Comfortable working hands-on with laboratory equipment and technical test samples.



**Preferred Qualifications**

* Experience with waveguide optics, diffractive optics, AR/VR displays, grating couplers, or nanophotonic devices;
* Experience with optical modeling, RCWA simulations, ray tracing, or correlation of simulations to physical measurements;
* Experience with nanoimprint lithography, spin coating, thin-film deposition, wafer processing, laser cutting, or optical assembly;
* Experience characterizing refractive index, transmission, reflectance, absorption, haze, scattering, surface roughness, or flatness;
* Experience with glass, SiC, polymers, resins, hardcoats, anti-reflection coatings, or other optical materials;
* Familiarity with optical metrology systems, spectrometers, interferometric or profilometry tools, or custom measurement equipment;
* Experience developing mechanical, environmental, or reliability tests for optical components;
* Proficiency in developing and executing Finite Element Analysis (FEA) models for stress, deformation, thermal, mechanical, or reliability analysis of materials;
* Proficiency in Python, MATLAB, or equivalent tools for data analysis and technical automation;
* Experience creating or reviewing CAD, DXF, wafer-layout, or supplier-manufacturing data;
* Experience working with external suppliers on technical requirements, sample plans, process development, and qualification.

If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please don’t be shy and provide us some information.

"Default Together" Policy at Snap: At Snap Inc. we believe that being together in person helps us build our culture faster, reinforce our values, and serve our community, customers and partners better through dynamic collaboration. To reflect this, we practice a “default together” approach and expect our team members to work in an office 4+ days per week. 

At Snap, we believe that having a team of diverse backgrounds and voices working together will enable us to create innovative products that improve the way people live and communicate. Snap is proud to be an equal opportunity employer, and committed to providing employment opportunities regardless of race, religious creed, color, national origin, ancestry, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, childbirth and breastfeeding, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other protected classification, in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local laws. EOE, including disability/vets.

Our Benefits: Snap Inc. is its own community, so we’ve got your back! We do our best to make sure you and your loved ones have everything you need to be happy and healthy, on your own terms. Our benefits are built around your needs and include paid parental leave, comprehensive medical coverage, emotional and mental health support programs, and compensation packages that let you share in Snap’s long-term success!

Waterman Infrastructure & Environment are recruiting for a Geo-Environmental Engineer to join the team based in Manchester, UK. This is a full-time, permanent position. The Ground Engineering team provides geoenvironmental consultancy and geotechnical design services to a range of external clients including developers, house-builders, local authorities and contractors. Waterman prides itself on providing its staff with a rewarding and challenging career, encouraging Continuous Professional Development and allowing employees to reach their full potential.

**Responsibilities:**

* Supporting a variety of geo-environmental projects for both external clients and for other teams within Waterman;
* Supervising ground investigations;
* Preparing Preliminary Risk Assessments (Desk studies);
* Soil logging to current UK standards, including laboratory scheduling;
* Completing soil sampling, water monitoring and sampling;
* Writing interpretative ground investigation reports;
* Input to the design of remediation works and geotechnical design;
* Knowledge of contaminated land legislation and reporting requirements;
* Reviewing and interpreting factual site investigation data; and,
* Travel to other offices and sites within the UK (as needed).

**Qualification and Experience:**

* BSc or equivalent in Geology, Environmental Science or similar;
* Working towards membership of a relevant professional body with a longer-term goal to move toward chartership with a relevant institution;
* Basic knowledge of planning legislation;
* Experience of site inspections and reporting;
* Able to complete interpretative assessments to a basic level;
* Able to deliver projects and work within a multi-disciplinary consultancy;
* Track record in managing time and resources effectively and within budget; and.
* In possession of full UK driving license.

**What's on Offer**

* Competitive salary and benefits package with annual salary reviews.
* 26 days' holiday per year, rising to 31 days with loyalty days, plus bank holidays.
* Hybrid working arrangements.
* Fantastic training and development culture.
* Access to mentoring and support from industry experts.
* Opportunity to lead exciting and varied projects across multiple sectors.
* Significant client-facing responsibility.
* Opportunity to contribute to business development and help grow existing and new client relationships.
* Strong opportunities for career progression within Waterman Group.
